Ladybird’s drawingBufferWidth and drawingBufferHeight report the canvas
size clamped to between 1 and the largest the drawing buffer supports,
which is the size the buffer is allocated at. The other engines do the
same: Blink’s WebGLRenderingContextBase::ClampedCanvasSize() clamps each
dimension to between 1 and the maximum viewport dimension, and its
drawingBufferWidth() reads the size of the drawing buffer. WebKit’s
clampedCanvasSize() constrains the size between 1x1 and the maximum
viewport dimensions. And Gecko’s ClientWebGLContext::SetDimensions()
makes a width or height of 0 into 1.
